    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. The change is complete.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec asked that a successful owner create emit an AUDIT log line with the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\nI found that a production emitter class `AuditOwnerCreated` already existed and logged exactly those three fields to the `AUDIT` logger \u2014 but it was **dead code**, never referenced by any YAML pipeline. The `POST /api/owners` pipeline ended `save \u2192 respond`, so no audit line was ever emitted and `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` would fail.\n\nTwo edits:\n\n1. **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the pre-existing class matched the requirement, but to keep it robust and self-contained I (re)wrote it as a proper `@Val Owner` step that logs id/customerCode/registrationDate to `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`.\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond`, so it runs *after* `save` (which assigns the owner id) and carries the same `transaction` governance as the rest of the pipeline:\n\n```yaml\nsave:\n  ...\n  next: audit\n\naudit:\n  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.AuditOwnerCreated\n  govern: [ transaction ]\n  next: respond\n```\n\n## Verification\n\n- Target test `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` \u2014 passes; the run logged `AUDIT - Owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-07`.\n- Full `./mvnw test` \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (this project's only test), **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
